{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Go driver CRUD, bson.D versus bson.M and struct tags",
  "slug": "go-driver-crud-bson-d-versus-bson-m-and-struct-tags",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:a62e0f6fe0121791dfc108855ec50c7f1682c13976088616343c1b1060d94824",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "8d4f971c0d2feb4c86fbd9161b54bf22c80acc26418a5c50e25d1d42f5d19d91",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:96ebdb8aa399bf3a32fb99d366bc21a671f47c1460bf3b687b787c93fa6c388f",
      "text": "`UpdateOne` changes at most one matching document and requires a nonempty update document containing update operators. `ReplaceOne` replaces at most one matching document and its replacement must not contain update operators. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/mongo/collection.go",
      "also": [
        "https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/how-to-use-mongodb-with-go/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5af9cfa2b3817303d9248099ab9be5666fd7bef95cdc8e3b1638da477b4b5ef3",
        "ev:f95e433efb5e11547f47254109ceccdb6f70bc6fd7100d870a86ff5d947dbd1b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:518bc3b3e292f06724a3a551f6ae7fc6eb70a704cf21ae947a955b8a9ecd138d",
      "text": "Setting `UseJSONStructTags` enables fallback to a `json` tag when a `bson` tag is absent. The documented client configuration applies BSON options through `SetBSONOptions`. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/mongo/options/clientoptions.go",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/bson.md",
        "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:885f535db668784bcb12c101c5c9e86227d605651d48d095d98be2dc388d0995",
        "ev:918ff93c49d882ffda075c4fa79a2d546223ada087618b4475e9cac37e3ca808"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:91c26927001367ab0475dcdf6cc89621f3a08637d37da8baccd891ab139ab24c",
      "text": "A BSON struct tag specifies a BSON field name and optional comma-separated options. The bson:\"restaurant_id,omitempty\" tag renames RestaurantId and omits it when empty. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/struct-tagging.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3bb20c7bbc59bae10231ced0d29d7dcc794fbaa6c85bde296dae20ebc696e74d",
        "ev:ebfa8e79e1ade2dd8fc61f30ad35c3f250550585d27ad548413b8c180b5749c4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a00536a7b9260232795451c05bdddb6fd8b981baa6ac0a64e1965e78dea41bf9",
      "text": "minsize stores supported integer fields as BSON int32 when their values fit, otherwise retaining BSON int64. truncate permits fractional BSON doubles to be truncated when decoding into non-float numeric fields. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/bson.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:32b722622e407067514f92750a6dcbf22cfa6fda690fac9505fe67bec88fd9f5",
        "ev:4754bce57d54f21c0130d7ff78be62668151b928f8c5fd4fce8b55d3b57a62ec"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bcc332433d20409d5fa03f201e7d70b7a785f92535cb263becc18f017c6101ce",
      "text": "Avoid duplicate field names in bson.D: the BSON API documentation warns that duplicate key names can cause undefined server behavior. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b851c6f30a4df2e14ab1b413111430b48aa00e822da017e2ff65a05e7d3cf656"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3e54bc1fbe30306ac555bfca2509fe99f23d55ddee2d5b62d435cff5dd9d6f3c",
      "text": "A nil `bson.D` used as a sort document can trigger a `WriteNull` error in CRUD marshaling. The driver troubleshooting guide distinguishes `var sort bson.D` from an initialized empty `bson.D{}`. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/docs/common-issues.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:25bf269c7109885c575991501746124937736de67f84ede65102965df8c228f0",
        "ev:56f8b8f0b086039572ed77212312a523e30f92a3ac4c215089d05b44aa1c96b2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9f508a253c78cc5f3b14963e6e9789337d1136760de80d8045a960f8fd14af99",
      "text": "`bson.M` does not provide stable field order: the driver serializes its elements in undefined order, consistent with the Go language specification leaving map iteration order unspecified. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [
        "https://go.dev/ref/spec",
        "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/bson/primitive.go"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3e6efdcd34eb0ef7a3ba9d5b0bbb19628baa568558849aa93fddcd0b4dba74fd",
        "ev:f2481238059938cc485b6e2e100a9c378de716a71cec46d2862e207773701255"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bdd84be86e98b5697123b0ed0f6a44dc41b94aa2123552d3b22c6c6bc5100459",
      "text": "Only exported struct fields participate in default BSON marshaling and unmarshaling. Default keys lowercase Go field names; BSON struct tags override the stored field name. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/bson.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/struct-tagging.md",
        "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4e9a0134574370e7e1b9c0b3c96f1764a39787ae890ce65f60e603627ded8e3e",
        "ev:edadd53ed17c5d152129778bf261e1282a499cd702a47fd7cd58cb6adaf9da33"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0d6e58f520a8aed90384a20ea5c627ebe12ae5217a9da118351bb4405242d253",
      "text": "`InsertOne` accepts a struct document and applies its BSON tags during insertion; the struct-tag example inserts a `Restaurant` with a custom `restaurant_id` key and omits empty tagged fields. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/struct-tagging.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/mongo/collection.go",
        "https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/how-to-use-mongodb-with-go/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5d0d1173f9654595e5522067e1d8e177e6c284494f31ab965c24210192b3218f",
        "ev:9a99a9c0adedafca80c83f311fad4e1371fb1dacb2edb83a6b4e1cf456a65f16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0c39fed614ada4b567c541e2805f9dc913c342517fc92054109ed6e61c664f3e",
      "text": "`DeleteOne` removes at most one matching document. A successful no-match delete reports `DeletedCount` equal to `0`; a successful no-match `UpdateOne` reports `MatchedCount` equal to `0`. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/mongo/collection.go",
      "also": [
        "https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/how-to-use-mongodb-with-go/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0e304d21681f06c413e650e26f4b2b14474dd91afa5a46d10021034ee75949a3",
        "ev:3ce9a2194765b1504815cc41410cad793fb4c7e4798383b8ab204befbfa08e79",
        "ev:5fe03dcf8a8f03595d5bce7e207598369d1d2f80dfddbae5bca383206505954e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:35a62f11a10dc0b5238f518889d31d67d853293d4677714595041fa0747b5699",
      "text": "omitempty omits zero-valued numbers, booleans and strings, zero-length slices, maps and arrays, and nil pointers or interfaces. By default a struct is empty only if it implements Zeroer and IsZero returns true; ordinary structs are not automatically omitted. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:ce5fa5819cee4e0912f6a8002f8ac77ceaf177798b4dc19a4feb2919989f9d93"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:723214c712294ef311b9d45427e73aa81021f4034e05599a08a5381731eddb9e",
      "text": "The `inline` BSON tag flattens a struct or map field into its containing BSON document and reverses that flattening during unmarshaling. Untagged embedded struct fields instead become subdocuments. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/bson.md",
      "also": [
        "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:43322c75b606783ec81dadf296f18952220a1d1f972fa621a596112d6d29861a",
        "ev:aa21dfcbaa0a669bf15881b11a870d121fee292e56d5cb9bdd4a7d487000cd7b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c24a5c74ee2300a5e676a737dc23bce0b55da60cc56a8b2792097614b7a9d237",
      "text": "Scope unordered-filter advice carefully: equality against an entire embedded document requires an exact match including field order. A Go user thread illustrates intermittent misses with nested `bson.M`, whereas ordered `bson.D` preserves the equality document order. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/query-embedded-documents.md",
      "also": [
        "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/75253113/mongodb-golang-findone-with-nested-bson-m-failed-for-10-attempts-bson-mbso",
        "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6a13400d03022b5985d92cd6a8db78166e36a98c6734a14db4156eaa76707959",
        "ev:8d98de0ff75d8e9dbcfbf3fbb53f95b13c1c28c40ca7b76eb24439f6fbc04a11",
        "ev:c0b39dca7e526a445e1104f7010389e291e4da746c63d79f7398cd9147996fd7",
        "ev:f8fdf7302ddbedaefb08d426b5e1f23f5a99a7c10ec2c23b9dcc2213ce6b7586"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0fc14b413cbc4e4f4b006077e8f8a1b8fb3edda27831031697286b2a5dc7245f",
      "text": "The community discussion distinguishes field order inside a BSON document from element order in an outer slice: `[]bson.M` preserves slice element order while each map remains unordered. For multiple sort fields, the discussion recommends `bson.D` to preserve sort precedence. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/66272948/is-order-of-array-of-bson-m-maintained-in-mongodb-go-driver",
      "also": [
        "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/64281675/bson-d-vs-bson-m-for-find-queries"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1dea83cd8d310ab84963bf31b5a9b263166744a5fab9633c0f36783c7b9f2d44",
        "ev:3dc7d88644ae1e9eff2b1ab96a9c66342e81f94b94680cf6fcaa1044a661643d",
        "ev:7f50f9034908214a0afd2f710b9b591bd98e2c8835a038a490cfd672c40421f6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:a603d6d69bc94b0f9dc1189aab778cb4601f4452d2d50374105cf25d3568b517",
      "text": "A nil pointer marshals as BSON null; a non-nil pointer marshals as its underlying type. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pkg.go.dev/go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2/bson",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/go/current/data-formats/bson.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
